,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.953854888,"data":"READING THIS OUTPUT\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.954638088,"data":"  * The three selftest_* entries gate everything. If any says FAIL, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.95532641,"data":"    numbers below it are not trustworthy and the harness is the suspect.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.956020784,"data":"  * Each entry also gates on a DDA step count. An entry that reports a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.95679291,"data":"    throughput but a mean of ~1.000 steps/pixel is NOT a voxel-render\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.95748308,"data":"    measurement: the render exited on its first voxel test every pixel.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.958157902,"data":"    bench.cu refuses to report timings for such a config unless\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.958883115,"data":"    --measure-degenerate is passed, which is used exactly once here, for the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.95962291,"data":"    entry that exists to document the pre-fix baseline.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.96032862,"data":"  * env-steps/s is batch / median_us. A whole-step number, not a per-kernel one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.961037989,"data":"  * The measured memory floors in each log are the denominators. %-of-floor\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.961784234,"data":"    figures only mean something against a floor measured on the same card.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.962524919,"data":"  * The author's 49.6M is an RTX 3090 claim. This is a T4. They are not\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":97.96324922,"data":"    comparable numbers and must not be differenced directly.\n"}
